      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "1. I took a print on 2025-01-01:\n\n(from the metadata)\n\n<xmp:CreateDate>2026-01-01T23:09:31.1942695+09:00</xmp:CreateDate>\n\n2. Found I forgot to add the message so I edited it right away after the automated print. I also downloaded it today so I can post it on SNS, only found the time was altered:\n\n<xmp:CreateDate>2026-01-02T08:09:47.0000000+09:00</xmp:CreateDate>\n\n(*Now my new year print is less worthily :<)*My assumption, issue is the print-message system, it added the timezone when applying the messages*\n\n3. To test the assumption, I deleted one of my 64 prints and took a new print, it should be 1904, the metadata of the automated save to the print was correct: \n\n<xmp:CreateDate>2026-01-04T19:04:02.5828570+09:00</xmp:CreateDate>\n\n4. I want to process to download the new print manually to check the metadata, but instantly found the automated print was already in the wrong displayed date(of tomorrow):2026-01-05\n\n5. Downloaded the print, the metadata suggest it's \"NOW+my timezone(+9)\":\n\n<xmp:CreateDate>2026-01-05T04:04:03.0000000+09:00</xmp:CreateDate>\n\n6. Edited the photo and download from the UI, no change:\n\n<xmp:CreateDate>2026-01-05T04:04:03.0000000+09:00</xmp:CreateDate>\n\n7. Print and then download the edited print, no change:\n\n<xmp:CreateDate>2026-01-05T04:04:03.0000000+09:00</xmp:CreateDate>\n\nConclusion: It's not the add-message system, it's the print processing, there's a bug, when server process the print, it will add the timezone right away",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
